# FIX51 (docs/runbook/FIX51.md, "Round 3 measurements"): the rendered rate of a
# timedemo of demo1.dm2 (its fps line) in the Metal shim build of ref_gl1, 5120x2880 vid_fullscreen 1, r_vsync 0,
# with the stock game settings and metal_stats 1 (the presented and the
# drawable-less frames, counted over the whole run, at the renderer's close).
# TASK161: the engine's metal_rate line adds FIX51's presented a second over a
# window (from metal_rate_start, 1 s, after the first frame), reported as the
# metric presented_rate beside fps, and the frames that found every present
# slot held as held.
# The headline is the presented rate: FIX68's frames-in-flight cap makes this
# shim render fewer frames nobody sees (fps falls) while the presented count
# holds or rises, so fps stays a secondary metric. Its stored baseline holds
# no presented rate: this headline needs a new baseline (TASK161 runbook).
adapter=quake2
description=FIX51 presents: gl1-metal, 5120x2880 vid_fullscreen 1, r_vsync 0, timedemo of demo1.dm2
targets=client game ref_gl1
build_flags=WITH_METAL_SHIM=yes
settings=renderer=gl1-metal size=5120x2880 fullscreen=1 vsync=0 pace=timedemo seconds=8 cvar.metal_stats=1
requires=physical-gpu
runs=3
warmup=1
wall=40
metric=presented_rate
better=higher
abs_tol=1
rel_tol=0.1
accept=0
